   "answer": "The spillover matrix is computed. The four controls are FL1-H, FL2-H, FL3-H and FL4-H. Each coefficient is the share of a control's signal that appears in another channel. The diagonal is 1.\n\n**What I did**\n1. I read the procedure for spillover and percent-positive work.\n2. I ran the spillover step on the four single-stain controls, using compdata_060909_001.fcs as the unstained control.\n3. I read the saved matrix file (spillover.csv).\n\n**Settings used**\n- Method: median method. For each control, the median of the positive events minus the median of the unstained control, divided by the same difference in the primary channel.\n- Positive events: the events above the 80th percentile of the unstained control in the primary channel. The 80th percentile came from the decision record.\n- Scale: the instrument writes log-amplified channel numbers. The decades setting comes from the decision record. The tool output does not echo the value it used. See the uncertainties below.\n- Scatter gate: the tool output does not state the gate. The value from the decision record applies.\n- Software: flowCore 4.6.1.\n- Controls: 4 single-stain files, one for each channel. One control is one replicate.\n\n**Off-diagonal coefficients (control channel first)**\n\n1. FL1-H into FL2-H: 0.242\n2. FL1-H into FL3-H: 0.032\n3. FL1-H into FL4-H: 0.0011\n4. FL2-H into FL1-H: 0.0077\n5. FL2-H into FL3-H: 0.141\n6. FL2-H into FL4-H: 0.0027\n7. FL3-H into FL1-H: 0.015\n8. FL3-H into FL2-H: 0.176\n9. FL3-H into FL4-H: 0.230\n10. FL4-H into FL1-H: 0.00076\n11. FL4-H into FL2-H: 0.00096\n12. FL4-H into FL3-H: 0.0032\n\nThe full-precision values are in spillover.csv. The largest off-diagonal coefficient is 0.242 (FL1-H into FL2-H). The tool reports a maximum residual after compensation of 0.032.\n\n**What I found**\n- The largest spillovers are FL1-H into FL2-H (0.242), FL3-H into FL4-H (0.230) and FL3-H into FL2-H (0.176).\n- FL4-H spills very little into the other channels. Its coefficients are all below 0.004.\n- No coefficient is above 1. The four controls have four different primary channels.\n\n**What is uncertain**\n- I could not confirm that the log decades were applied. The tool output does not show the decades value. The data are log-amplified, so a wrong decades value would change every coefficient. Please check the decades value in the decision record.\n- The positive cutoff is the 80th percentile of the unstained control. Other cutoffs change the median of the positive events and so change the coefficients. I did not test other cutoffs.\n- I could not read the file headers. The inspection tool failed with a permission error, so I did not check the channel names or the header values.\n- One control per channel gives no estimate of spread. I cannot give a confidence interval.\n\n**What waits for you**\n- Confirm the log decades value (the data are four decades over 1024 channels, so 4 is expected).\n- Confirm the 80th percentile positive cutoff and the scatter gate, if you want other values. I can run the matrix again with other values using compare_options.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Cutoff for positive events in a control: 80 · Decades of a log-amplified scale: 4 · Parent gate on scatter: none.",
